    introHeading: "What is Assessments?",
    intro: ["A mental health assessment is a structured evaluation of your emotional, behavioral, and psychological well-being. It brings together your story, your symptoms, your medical and family history, and your goals, so that a clinician can understand what you are experiencing and recommend appropriate next steps. For many people in Tooele, it is the first step toward feeling better and the moment when scattered concerns finally make sense together.","Assessments can help adults and others who are dealing with depression, anxiety, trauma-related symptoms, attention difficulties, mood instability, or changes in thinking and behavior. They are also valuable when you have been treated before but are not sure the original diagnosis fits, or when symptoms overlap with medical conditions, medications, or sleep problems that deserve a closer look.","The approach is grounded in widely accepted clinical practice. Diagnostic interviews, based on established criteria, are often combined with validated screening tools such as questionnaires for depression and anxiety. Research consistently shows that accurate diagnosis and early identification lead to better matching of treatment to the individual, and that measuring symptoms over time helps guide care."],
    signsHeading: "Common signs an assessment may help",
    signsList: ["Persistent sadness, irritability, or loss of interest in daily activities","Ongoing worry, panic, or physical tension that is hard to control","Changes in sleep, appetite, energy, or concentration","Difficulty with focus, organization, or follow-through at work or school","Mood swings or periods of unusually high energy","Distressing memories, nightmares, or feeling constantly on edge","Withdrawal from relationships or trouble functioning at home","Uncertainty about whether what you are experiencing has a name or a treatment"],
    bullets: ["A comprehensive conversation about your concerns, history, medications, sleep, substance use, and daily functioning","Screening questionnaires may be used to add structure and help track change over time","Findings explained in plain language, including possible diagnoses and options","A personalized plan that may include medication management, psychotherapy, lifestyle strategies, or referrals for further testing","Follow-up visits to review progress and adjust the plan"],
