    introHeading: "What is Medication Management?",
    intro: ["Medication management is the ongoing clinical care of psychiatric medication. It includes deciding whether a medication is appropriate, choosing a starting dose, monitoring how you respond, and making adjustments over time. It is more than a prescription: it is a continuing conversation between you and your prescriber about how you feel and function.","It can help people with depression, anxiety disorders, bipolar disorder, ADHD, sleep difficulties, and other mental health conditions. Many people come to us after starting a medication elsewhere and want a careful review. Others are considering medication for the first time and want clear, honest information before deciding.","Research supports the use of medication for many psychiatric conditions, particularly when it is monitored regularly and combined with therapy and healthy routines. Responses differ widely from person to person, which is why regular follow-up matters. Careful monitoring helps catch side effects early and ensures treatment keeps pace with your life. For people in Tooele and nearby communities, local, consistent care can make that follow-up easier to maintain."],
    signsHeading: "Signs medication management may help",
